---
const profilePicture = 'https://i.imgur.com/umBZPqd.png';
---

<section>
  <div class='profile'>
    <img
      alt="bycarlosgamez's website"
      class='profile__picture'
      src={profilePicture}
      height='200px'
      width='200px'
    />

    <div class='profile__details'>
      <h1>Carlos Gamez</h1>
      <h2 class='accent'>
        I design systems and build in the browser to solve the right problems,
        not just ship features.
      </h2>
      <p>
        I’m a designer who codes, not to be an engineer, but because code is my
        favorite design tool. I love the technical side and know my way around
        front-end development, but I always start with the user. I use Figma to
        explore and document ideas, but I bring them to life in the browser. I
        care about craft, usability, and building things that solve problems.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .profile {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: center;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    padding: 1rem 0 3rem 0;
  }

  .profile__details {
    flex: 1 0 300px;
  }

  .profile__details > h1 {
    margintop: 0;
  }

  .profile__picture {
    border-radius: 50%;
    margin: 0 2rem 1rem 0;
  }

  .accent {
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  h2 {
    font-weight: bold;
  }
  p {
    color: var(--grey-400);
    line-height: 1.5rem;
  }
</style>
